{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And Abraham said: I, and so forth.</b> Meaning: I have a reply to your claim in which you said ״כַּחֶסֶד״ and so forth — but I desire the matter; I will swear." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that since he wished to reprove him concerning the well of water, as stated shortly below (Genesis 21:25), he was concerned that he might think his reply was meant to undermine his kindness and to avoid swearing. Therefore he prefaced by saying <b>I will swear</b>, and afterward reproved him concerning and so forth." "<b>Further,</b> he intends to say <b>I will swear</b> — meaning: on my own behalf; no harm has come to you and so forth — and he intends to exclude an obligation upon his son." "<b>Or</b> it may intend that he himself will swear and cause his sons to swear regarding these three generations, and the vowel points will prove it:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:39.239533211Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}